WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:04.810
Buckle your seatbelts and hold on tight, as
we ramp up to 88 miles per hour and break

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:08.800
down the entire time-traveling adventure story
of the Back to the Future trilogy.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.380
There's not a lot we know about the original
version of 1885 before Marty and Doc started

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:18.790
messing with it, but we do know one vitally
important event that happens: Clara Clayton

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:21.500
was hired to be the new teacher at the Hill
Valley school.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.650
She had just arrived at the Hill Valley train
station, loaded up her wagon with her possessions,

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.420
and was heading to her new home when a snake
spooked her horses.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.140
She lost control of her wagon, and her horses
took off galloping toward Shonash Ravine.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.460
After careening into the ravine, Clara died
without ever making it to her teaching post.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:40.250
Clayton Ravine wound up being named after
her, and the story of her death became an

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:41.880
urban legend at Hill Valley High.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.010
"Every kid at school knows that story because
we all have teachers we'd like to see fall

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:45.600
into the ravine."

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:51.420
In Hill Valley during the fall of 1955, a
teenage George McFly is up in a tree using

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.780
a pair of binoculars to watch his high school
crush Lorraine Baines change in her bedroom

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.980
when he falls out into the road and is hit
by a car.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:03.010
The driver of the car turns out to be Lorraine's
father, who ... not realizing that George

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:07.100
was peeping through his daughter's window
... brings George into their house to recuperate.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.170
Lorraine finds herself attracted to George,
drawn in by his apparent helplessness, and

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:15.450
the two decide to attend the Enchantment Under
the Sea Dance together, where they kiss for

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.450
the first time.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.520
However, Lorraine is also pursued by Biff
Tannen, another teen in their high school

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.920
class who bullies George relentlessly.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:27.330
Although Lorraine chooses George, Biff remains
fixated on her, and works to make George's

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.420
life more miserable as a result.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:33.830
On November 5, shortly before Lorraine and
George meet, Dr. Emmett "Doc" Brown slips

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:38.799
off his toilet while hanging a clock, bangs
his head, and is temporarily knocked unconscious.

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:42.760
When he comes to, he's had a vision of an
invention called a flux capacitor, which is

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.470
what makes time travel possible.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:48.420
On November 12, the clock tower at the Hill
Valley courthouse is struck by lightning.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:53.320
The original Back to the Future film begins
in 1985, where George and Lorraine are now

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.110
married and live in a modest suburban home
in Hill Valley.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:02:01.240
At work, George reports to Biff, who continues
to bully him and creepily hit on Lorraine.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.460
Instead of doing his homework, George has
now graduated to doing Biff's reports for

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:05.040
him.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:08.920
Lorraine's brother Joey is in jail, and has
failed to make his parole for at least the

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:09.640
second time.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:13.840
George and Lorraine have three children: Dave,
who is in his early 20s and works at Burger

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:19.240
King; Linda, who is around 19 and single,
and their youngest, Marty, who is 17 and dreams

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.080
of being a rock star.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.230
Marty's best friend is the eccentric scientist
Doc Brown, and he has a serious girlfriend

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:33.860
named Jennifer, of whom Marty's mother doesn't
approve.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:38.980
"I don't like it, Marty. Any girl who calls a boy is just asking for trouble!"

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:44.000
After 30 years of refining his initial design,
Doc finally perfects the flux capacitor and

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.349
builds a time machine out of a DeLorean.

00:02:46.349 --> 00:02:50.940
Because his invention requires a huge amount
of energy, he lies to a group of Libyan terrorists,

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:54.770
promising that he'll build them a bomb with
the stolen plutonium they supply and instead

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:57.870
giving them a bomb casing filled with pinball
machine parts.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:01.970
As Doc conducts the first test of his time
machine at the Twin Pines mall, the terrorists

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:03.450
arrive and shoot him dead.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:07.390
In an effort to escape from the terrorists,
Marty jumps into the DeLorean and accidentally

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:08.540
travels back in time.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:14.120
Arriving in 1955, Marty crashes into a pine
tree and winds up in a barn.

00:03:14.129 --> 00:03:17.710
After hiding the time machine, Marty walks
into town, where he sees a boy about to be

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:20.480
hit by a car and rushes to push him out of
the way.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:23.480
The car hits Marty instead, and the driver
brings him inside, after which Marty realizes

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:27.569
that the boy he saved was his father, and
that instead of becoming attracted to George,

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:31.180
Lorraine is now attracted to Marty, who goes
by the alias Calvin Klein.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:35.959
Determined to restore the timeline, Marty
seeks out the advice of the 1955 version of

00:03:35.959 --> 00:03:39.019
Doc, who has just had his vision of the flux
capacitor.

00:03:39.019 --> 00:03:42.659
Doc instructs him to do whatever he has to
do in order to get his parents together before

00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:45.519
Marty's timeline is completely erased from
existence.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:49.140
In the process, Marty's intervention gives
George the idea for a sci-fi novel.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.970
Marty's plan to push his parents together
results in George standing up to Biff for

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:56.739
the first time, and a newly confident George
finally kisses Lorraine.

00:03:56.739 --> 00:04:00.530
Meanwhile, Marty gives Chuck Berry the idea
to write the song "Johnny B. Goode," three

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:03.380
years before the song was composed in the
original timeline.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.900
Marty and Doc take advantage of the clock
tower lightning strike to create the power

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:11.960
needed to run the flux capacitor, harnessing
the lightning so Marty can return to 1985.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:16.980
Before Marty departs, he writes Doc a letter
warning him of his death in 1985, but Doc

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:21.940
rips the letter up, saying that the consequences
of knowing his own future could be disastrous.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:26.220
Marty decides to set the time of his return
to a few minutes earlier than he left, hoping

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:27.800
he'll be able to save Doc.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:31.520
However, by the time he arrives at the mall
... now Lone Pine Mall, thanks to the tree

00:04:31.539 --> 00:04:36.669
Marty crashed into in 1955 ... he's too late,
and watches Doc get shot again.

00:04:36.669 --> 00:04:41.220
However, after the terrorists depart and Marty
approaches Doc's body, Doc sits up, revealing

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.300
that he's wearing a bulletproof vest.

00:04:43.809 --> 00:04:47.999
Stunned, Marty asked how he knew; Doc admits
that he let curiosity get the best of him,

00:04:47.999 --> 00:04:50.199
and taped Marty's letter back together.

00:04:50.199 --> 00:04:53.999
Marty returns home to find his family significantly
better off than he left them.

00:04:53.999 --> 00:04:57.319
George is now a published science fiction
novelist, and he and Lorraine are healthier

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.560
and much more flirtatious than they were in
the original timeline.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.440
While they still live in the same house, the
decor has received an upgrade, although Marty's

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:05.440
room remains the same.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:10.000
Biff now owns an auto shop, and is responsible
for the detailing on the McFly cars.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:13.569
Instead of a Burger King, Dave now works in
an office, and while we still don't know much

00:05:13.569 --> 00:05:17.520
about Linda's life, she's at least dating
a lot, which seems to speak to her increased

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:18.100
self-confidence.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:22.380
Perhaps thanks to her own altered high school
dating experience, Lorraine now loves Jennifer,

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.780
and the McFlys have purchased Marty a black
pickup truck, which they expect him to take

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.320
on his weekend trip with her.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:32.130
We never see what would've originally happened
in the original 2015 timeline before Marty

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:36.650
traveled back to 1955 the first time, and
we actually never get to learn exactly how

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:39.420
things play out in the first new timeline
he creates either.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:44.920
The first perspective of 2015 that we get
is Doc's, whose presence in 2015 causes yet

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.240
another timeline to branch off.

00:05:46.629 --> 00:05:49.900
However, odds are that most of this new timeline
was very similar.

00:05:49.909 --> 00:05:54.460
In this timeline, after graduating high school,
Marty was going to pursue a career in music,

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:59.819
but finds his rock star dreams thwarted due
to a hand injury sustained during a car accident.

00:05:59.819 --> 00:06:03.740
Eventually, Marty and Jennifer get married
in the Chapel O' Love and have two children,

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:05.259
Marlene and Marty Junior.

00:06:05.259 --> 00:06:10.699
In 2015, Marty Jr. agrees to help Biff's grandson,
Griff Tannen, rob the Hill Valley Payroll

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:11.580
Substation.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.900
He's apprehended by police, and sentenced
to 15 years in prison.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:18.560
Marlene then attempts to break him out, and
she is sentenced to 20 years.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:22.980
Doc witnesses all of this during his visit,
and takes a newspaper to help him track alterations

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:23.980
to the timeline.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:28.580
He also gets a hover conversion for the DeLorean
which allows the car to fly, replaces the

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:33.409
DeLorean's energy source with a Mr. Fusion
portable nuclear reactor, and puts his dog,

00:06:33.409 --> 00:06:38.389
Einstein, into a suspended animation kennel
... which honestly seems pretty risky, considering

00:06:38.389 --> 00:06:40.000
that he's about to reset the whole timeline
again.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:46.200
Just as everything seems perfect for Marty
in 1985, Doc returns from 2015 and informs

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:49.060
Marty and Jennifer that their future children
need their help.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:53.800
The three of them pile into the DeLorean ... which
can now fly, thanks to its alterations ... and

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.500
zip back to 2015, thus spinning off a third
alternate timeline.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:01.940
Biff sees them disappear, but can't make sense
of what he saw for another 30 years.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:06.539
In 2015, Jennifer is knocked unconscious while
Marty impersonates his son so he can avoid

00:07:06.539 --> 00:07:09.909
the payroll robbery, thus giving both of his
children a better fate.

00:07:09.909 --> 00:07:13.580
Thanks to Marty's intervention, Griff and
his gang are arrested instead.

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:17.779
Feeling lucky, Marty purchases a Grays Sports
Almanac, detailing the results of sporting

00:07:17.779 --> 00:07:21.939
events from 1950-2000, but Doc makes him throw
it away.

00:07:21.939 --> 00:07:27.069
However, recognizing the flying DeLorean from
1985, a much older Biff realizes that it's

00:07:27.069 --> 00:07:28.069
a time machine.

00:07:28.069 --> 00:07:32.699
Unbeknownst to Marty, Old Biff grabs the sports
almanac, and later steals the DeLorean.

00:07:32.699 --> 00:07:36.819
Meanwhile, Jennifer is brought to her future
home by well-meaning police officers who believe

00:07:36.819 --> 00:07:39.240
she's the 2015 version of herself.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:43.830
While hiding from her future family, she witnesses
the older Marty being fired by his boss after

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:46.789
agreeing to participate in an illegal scheme
with a coworker.

00:07:46.789 --> 00:07:51.319
Afterward, she reconnects with Marty and Doc,
and the trio ... plus Einstein, who's thankfully

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.400
fine ... return to 1985.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:58.800
Old Biff returns to November 5, 1955, the
same day Marty originally traveled to in the

00:07:58.819 --> 00:07:59.819
first movie.

00:07:59.819 --> 00:08:03.939
He tracks down the teenage Biff at his grandmother's
house and gives the Grays Sports Almanac to

00:08:03.939 --> 00:08:07.929
his younger self, instructing him to use it
to place bets on sporting events.

00:08:07.929 --> 00:08:13.089
At first, the younger Biff is skeptical, but
Old Biff convinces him of the almanac's authenticity

00:08:13.089 --> 00:08:17.129
by using it to predict the results of a live
event being reported on the radio.

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:21.319
After convincing teenage Biff of the almanac's
potential power, Old Biff instructs him to

00:08:21.319 --> 00:08:23.159
always keep it hidden and locked up.

00:08:23.159 --> 00:08:27.619
He also warns his younger self that at some
point in the future, a "kid" or a "crazy,

00:08:27.619 --> 00:08:31.770
wild-eyed old man who claims to be a scientist"
may show up asking about the book.

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:35.729
When that happens, Old Biff tells Young Biff
that he shouldn't hesitate to kill them.

00:08:35.729 --> 00:08:40.159
Old Biff then takes the DeLorean and returns
to 2015, leaving the almanac with his younger

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:40.760
self.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:45.020
Not long after, Biff uses the sports almanac
to place his first bet, and quickly starts

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:46.260
amassing a fortune.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:51.300
Sometime after Marty was born, Biff ... now
a billionaire, thanks to the almanac ... kills

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.380
George McFly and marries Lorraine.

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:58.120
He also starts a company called BiffCo, uses
his vast resources and influence to legalize

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:03.290
gambling in California, and builds himself
a 27-story casino in Hill Valley named Biff's

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:04.579
Pleasure Paradise.

00:09:04.579 --> 00:09:06.930
Biff's control doesn't end with his businesses,
though.

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:10.790
He also largely usurps control of the Hill
Valley Police Department, leading to Hill

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:12.380
Valley becoming a teeming crime hub.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:17.790
As for Lorraine's children, by 1985, Dave
has fallen into a life of crime, although

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:22.220
Biff pays to keep him out of jail; Linda lives
off of Biff's credit cards; and Marty is sent

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:23.720
to boarding school in Switzerland.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:28.410
Back in Hill Valley, Biff forces Lorraine
to get cosmetic surgery and she becomes an

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:28.960
alcoholic.

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:29.940
"Mom, it can't be you!"

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.140
"Yes it's me, Marty.

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:33.940
Are you alright?"

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:39.240
"I'm fine, I'm fine, it's just that you're
so… you're so… big."

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:44.360
This is the 1985 that Marty and Doc return
to, in which they quickly realize that something

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:46.120
in the past has gone horribly wrong.

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:51.260
Doc learns that the 1985-D version of himself
has been committed to a mental hospital, and

00:09:51.269 --> 00:09:52.990
that George McFly is dead.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:57.220
Marty confronts Biff, who readily admits everything
about the almanac and his killing of George,

00:09:57.220 --> 00:10:00.720
and also tells him exactly when he received
the almanac from his future self.

00:10:01.009 --> 00:10:04.700
Biff then attempts to shoot Marty with the
same gun that killed his father, but Marty

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.220
and Doc escape in the DeLorean.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:11.620
Marty and Doc travel back to 1955 to steal
the sports almanac back from younger Biff

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:12.860
and restore the timeline.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:17.959
Most events play out as they did in 1955-A,
since Doc and Marty have to be careful not

00:10:17.959 --> 00:10:21.940
to allow the other versions of themselves
from the first movie know they are there.

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:26.370
Marty manages to steal the almanac from Biff
after George knocks him unconscious, but Biff

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:27.680
later manages to steal it back.

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:32.600
Finally, Marty is able to retrieve the almanac
from Biff's car while he's driving it, resulting

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:34.310
in yet another car crash.

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:38.480
Doc implores Marty to burn the almanac, which
he does using a matchbook he'd taken from

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:44.000
Biff's Pleasure Paradise in 1985-D. As the
almanac burns, the logo on the matchbook changes

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:48.000
into the one for Biff's auto detailing business
from 1985-A.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:53.380
Satisfied that they've restored the timeline,
Marty and Doc prepare to return to 1985, but

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:57.649
before Doc can land the DeLorean and allow
Marty to climb in, the flying car is struck

00:10:57.649 --> 00:10:59.480
by lightning and disappears.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:04.860
Doc arrives in 1885, back in the earliest
days of Hill Valley, and finds that the time

00:11:04.871 --> 00:11:08.510
circuits of the DeLorean have been completely
fried by the lightning strike.

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:13.920
Lacking the technology to fix the time machine,
Doc realizes he's stranded in 1885, and builds

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:15.780
a new life for himself as a blacksmith.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:21.279
After spending some time in 1885, Doc decides
to hide the DeLorean in a mine shaft and leave

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:26.459
detailed instructions for Marty on how to
fix it in 1955, so he can return to 1985.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:32.000
"If the me of the future is now in the past,
how could you possibly know about it?"

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.160
"You sent me a letter."

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:39.440
Doc turns the letter over to the postal service,
instructing them on the exact location, date,

00:11:39.449 --> 00:11:42.600
and time that they'll be able to deliver it
to Marty in 1955.

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:47.139
In his letter, he gives Marty explicit instructions
not to return for him.

00:11:47.139 --> 00:11:52.019
One of Doc's jobs as a blacksmith is shoeing
a horse for Buford "Mad Dog" Tannen, Biff's

00:11:52.019 --> 00:11:54.420
ancestor, but Tannen then refuses to pay.

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:58.680
Afterward, the horse throws Tannen off, causing
him to break a $5 bottle of whiskey.

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:03.980
Tannen blames Doc for the incident, saying
he owes him $5 for the whiskey and $75 for

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:04.560
the horse.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:08.840
Shortly thereafter, Doc is asked by the mayor
to go meet the new schoolteacher at the train

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:12.740
station, leading him to save Clara Clayton
from her fall into the ravine.

00:12:13.060 --> 00:12:16.180
The two quickly fall in love, but their romance
is sadly short-lived.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:20.770
After getting his portrait taken in front
of the new courthouse clock, Doc is shot in

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:24.110
the back by Tannen while dancing with Clara
at the town festival.

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:28.329
He dies and is buried in Hill Valley, where
his grave is later discovered by Marty in

00:12:28.329 --> 00:12:31.249
1955 after receiving Doc's letter.

00:12:31.249 --> 00:12:32.360
"What's wrong, Marty?

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:33.860
You look like you've seen a ghost!"

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:36.400
"You're not far off, Doc."

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:42.680
After enlisting the help of the 1955-F Doc
to fix the recovered century-old time machine,

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:46.400
Marty travels back to 1885, despite Doc's
instructions.

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:51.261
However, Marty nicks the fuel line once he
arrives in 1885, causing the DeLorean to run

00:12:51.261 --> 00:12:52.290
out of gas.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:56.399
Although Doc challenges Marty's decision to
return for him, Marty explains that Doc has

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:57.780
only days left to live.

00:12:58.280 --> 00:13:01.950
Doc and Marty ... the latter of whom is now
using the alias "Clint Eastwood" ... begin

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:06.189
working together to try to figure out a way
to get the DeLorean up to the required 88

00:13:06.189 --> 00:13:08.020
miles per hour without fuel.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:12.040
"We'll stop it here, uncouple the cars from
the tender, throw the switch track, and then

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:16.920
we'll hijack ... borrow the locomotive, and
use it to push the time machine."

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:20.820
Aside from Doc and Marty's attempts to get
the time machine working, most events play

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:25.990
out as they did in 1885-F, up until the town
festival, when Marty saves Doc's life.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:31.149
Angry at Marty's interference, Mad Dog Tannen
challenges him to a duel in two days' time.

00:13:31.149 --> 00:13:34.890
Marty and Doc realize that they have to execute
their plan to travel back to the future before

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:37.180
then, and start preparing to hijack a train.

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:41.700
However, Doc becomes so despondent after saying
goodbye to Clara that he decides he won't

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:42.699
leave after all.

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:43.480
"Marty?"

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:44.480
"Yeah."

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:45.699
"I've made a decision."

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:46.700
"Uh-huh."

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:48.670
"I'm not going with you tomorrow.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:50.040
I'm staying here."

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:54.860
The following morning, a heartbroken Clara
buys a one-way train ticket out of Hill Valley,

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:57.589
while Marty is forced to face Tannen after
all.

00:13:57.589 --> 00:14:02.330
Using a trick from an old Clint Eastwood Western,
Marty manages to survive and incapacitate

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:06.480
Tannen, and he and Doc go to commandeer the
train, not realizing that Clara is on board.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:11.540
As the train approaches 88 miles per hour,
Doc chooses to save Clara rather than return

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:16.110
to the future with Marty, and as the train
soars off the track into the ravine, the DeLorean

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:17.240
travels through time again.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:22.560
Marty returns home for good, to a timeline
very much like the one he'd hoped to restore,

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:26.620
with the exception that the ravine is now
named "Eastwood Ravine," after he supposedly

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:28.999
perished in it in the past that he just left.

00:14:28.999 --> 00:14:34.290
No sooner has Marty arrived back in 1985 than
a modern train comes through, smashing the

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.790
DeLorean to bits while Marty jumps to safety.

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:40.559
Although it's bittersweet, Marty realizes
that this is what Doc wanted: to have the

00:14:40.559 --> 00:14:45.649
time traveling be over, the timeline secured,
Marty back home, and Doc with his true love.

00:14:45.649 --> 00:14:48.500
Marty reunites with Jennifer, and the two
of them go for a drive.

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:52.519
They're challenged to a race by Marty's future
criminal accomplice at a stoplight, but instead

00:14:52.519 --> 00:14:55.180
of racing, Marty puts his truck in reverse.

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:59.029
Watching a Rolls Royce cut into the would-be
path of his truck, Marty realizes he would

00:14:59.029 --> 00:15:03.449
have gotten into a devastating car accident,
which Jennifer realizes is the accident that

00:15:03.449 --> 00:15:05.020
would've cost him his music career.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:10.400
Looking at the fax from 2015-C in which Marty
was fired, Jennifer sees that it's been erased.

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:13.560
Marty and Jennifer head back to the site of
the wrecked DeLorean, and are shocked when

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:15.960
a flying locomotive engine appears out of
nowhere.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:20.800
It turns out that sometime after Marty traveled
back to the future, Doc stole another train

00:15:20.819 --> 00:15:24.889
and built a new time machine, which he and
Clara are using to travel throughout time.

00:15:24.889 --> 00:15:29.269
Doc reveals that he and Clara are now married
with two young sons, Jules and Verne, after

00:15:29.269 --> 00:15:30.720
their favorite science fiction author.

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:35.389
Doc urges Marty and Jennifer to make the best
futures possible, since nothing has yet been

00:15:35.389 --> 00:15:39.060
written, and then takes off in his train for
worlds ... and times ... unknown.

